{"name":"Baby Berries","hex":"#9c4a62","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.\n\nA very young human, even if not yet born.","A very young human, even if not yet born."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"berries","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of berry"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of berry"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/berries"}],"entries":[{"title":"Infant","blocks":[{"text":"An infant is a very young human being. Baby is an alternative term for infant. The terms may also be used to refer to juvenile beings of other organisms. A newborn is, in mainstream use, an infant who is only hours, days, or weeks old; while in medical contexts, a newborn or neonate is an infant in the first 28 days after birth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg/330px-The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infant"},{"title":"Berry","blocks":[{"text":"A berry is a small, pulpy, and often edible fruit. Typically, berries are juicy, rounded, brightly colored, sweet, sour or tart, and do not have a stone or pit although many pips or seeds may be present.‍ Common examples of berries in the culinary sense are strawberries, raspberries, blueberries, blackberries, white currants, blackcurrants, and redcurrants.‍ In Britain, soft fruit is a horticultural term for such fruits.‍"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Berberis_thunbergii_berries.jpg/330px-Be